打造了一个辉煌的成品环境。

134
00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:07.100
He was told at the time, this single episode's construction's costs were more than the first
当时有人告诉他，这一集的施工成本比前

135
00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:09.640
three or four seasons' costs combined.
三四季的总和还要多。

136
00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:10.620
Yes.
是的。

137
00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:15.840
Matt said he's also been very grateful to the episode's director, Charles McDougal, for his
马特说他也非常感谢这一集的导演查尔斯·麦克道格，感谢他的

138
00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:16.280
support.
支持。

139
00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:21.920
He said once they wrapped, Charles gave him a very fine bottle of wine and a card which
他说拍摄一结束，查尔斯就给了他一瓶非常好的红酒和一张卡片，上面

140
00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:25.700
read, we had no right to be able to get this episode shot last week.
写着：我们根本不可能在上周拍完这一集。

141
00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:29.300
You made the right call on the locations and designed them brilliantly.
你在选址上做了正确的决定，并且设计得非常出色。

142
00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:31.640
Thanks so much for all of the good work.
非常感谢你所做的一切出色工作。

143
00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.120
That's Charles McDougal right there.
这就是查尔斯·麦克道格。

144
00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:34.560
That's Charles McDougal.
这就是查尔斯·麦克道格。

145
00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:37.660
He works you hard, but he appreciates you.
他会让你工作得很辛苦，但他会赏识你。

146
00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:38.360
He sure does.
他确实会。

147
00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:44.440
Well, next up is Fast Fact 3, which I titled, Cringiest Episode.
好了，接下来是“冷知识3”，我给它起名叫“最尴尬的一集”。

148
00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:46.580
You brought this up earlier, Angela.
安吉拉，你之前提过这个。

149
00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:50.720
We got a fan mail flurry on this topic, actually.
事实上，我们收到了大量关于这个话题的粉丝来信。

150
00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:52.740
I'm going to read one from Melody S.
我要读一封来自梅洛迪·S的信。

151
00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:55.260
in Olive Branch, Mississippi, who said,
在密西西比州的奥利夫布兰奇，他说，

152
00:08:55.260 --> 00:09:00.280
I work in an office and thought how awkward it would be for me to be in a bathing suit with
我在办公室工作，想到要和所有只在办公室见过的同事一起穿泳装，

153
00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:03.440
all of my co-workers who I only see at the office.
那该有多尴尬啊。

154
00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:08.440
Was it weird and awkward for everyone to be in bathing suits in front of their co-workers?
大家在同事面前穿泳装，是不是既奇怪又尴尬？

155
00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:09.480
Yes.
是的。

156
00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:11.140
Yes, it was.
没错，确实如此。

157
00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:15.240
I mean, we weren't the cast of Baywatch.
我的意思是，我们又不是《海滩救护队》的演员。

158
00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:16.720
Okay, fine.
好吧，行吧。

159
00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:18.520
Baywatch, you hire me day one.
如果是《海滩救护队》，你第一天就雇了我。

160
00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:19.820
I'm in a bathing suit with you.
我和你一起穿着泳装。

161
00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:20.680
That's our outfit.
那是我们的工作服。

162
00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:21.660
That's what we wear.
我们平时就穿那个。

163
00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.980
I know what you look like in a bathing suit from day one.
从第一天起我就知道你穿泳装是什么样子。

164
00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:28.220
Not the case when you work at a paper company.
但在造纸公司工作可不是这样。

165
00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:32.680
So, you know, I was trading messages with Ellie Kemper about this episode,
所以，你知道，我当时正和艾丽·坎伯（Ellie Kemper）发消息聊这一集，

166
00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:36.860
and she sent in some audio clips, and the first one that she sent in,
她发来了一些音频片段，她发来的第一个片段，

167
00:09:36.960 --> 00:09:41.780
without me even asking her this question, was on this topic.
甚至在我还没问她这个问题之前，就是关于这个话题的。

168
00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:42.020
Yeah.
没错。

169
00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:42.940
Let's listen.
我们来听听。

170
00:09:44.400 --> 00:09:46.160
Hi, Jenna and Angela.
嗨，珍娜和安吉拉。

171
00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:47.180
This is Ellie.
我是艾丽。

172
00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:50.060
Okay, I have some thoughts about pool party.
好吧，我对《泳池派对》这一集有些想法。

173
00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:51.920
First of all, I loved that episode.
首先，我非常喜欢那一集。

174
00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:54.540
I don't know if you did, but I loved being on location.
我不知道你们喜不喜欢，但我很喜欢外景拍摄。

175
00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:58.400
I'm pretty sure we were in someone's actual house, right, with an indoor pool.
我很确定我们当时是在某人的真实住宅里，对吧，里面有个室内游泳池。

176
00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:00.260
So that was a ton of fun.
所以那真的超级有趣。

177
00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:03.340
I will tell you, I don't know if you had a similar reaction,
我得告诉你们，不知道你们有没有类似的反应，

178
00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:06.820
but when we did the table read the week before,
但当我们前一周进行剧本围读时，

179
00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:11.860
we found out we all had to be in swimsuits for a week.
我们发现大家都要穿一周的泳装。

180
00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:15.600
They gave us like five days notice, five days heads up.
他们只提前了五天通知我们，给了五天的准备时间。

181
00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:18.000
Okay, be swimsuit ready.
好吧，准备好穿泳装吧。

182
00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:22.900
I panicked because it was like, I'm pretty sure it was, I don't know, winter.
我当时很恐慌，因为我记得当时好像是冬天，我也不确定。

183
00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:27.840
It was not a time where you were thinking, oh, I'm going to be out on the beach in a swimsuit.
那根本不是你会想到“哦，我要去海滩穿泳装”的时候。

184
00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:32.680
So I remember like for three days, I did like push-ups and then stopped.
所以我记得我大概做了三天俯卧撑，然后就停了。

185
00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.660
Anyway, so that got me swimsuit ready.
总之，这就是我为穿泳装做的准备。

186
00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:37.400
Yes.
没错。

187
00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:38.580
I mean, that's bonkers.
我的天，这太疯狂了。

188
00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:42.300
That's something like, if you do a movie, you're like,
这就像是，如果你拍电影，你会知道，

189
00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:44.880
here's everything that's going to be required of me for this movie.
这部电影对我所有的要求都在这儿了。

190
00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:49.680
But when you're on a TV show, you learn the week before what's required of you the next week.
但当你拍电视剧时，你直到前一周才知道下周对你有什么要求。

191
00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:50.100
Yeah.
没错。

192
00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:52.100
So there's no prep time.
所以根本没有准备时间。

193
00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:54.260
I mean, we'll get into it.
我的意思是，我们之后会细聊。

194
00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:57.160
I had to wear a fake preggers belly in a bathing suit.
我当时还得戴着假孕肚穿泳装。

195
00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:58.660
I'm going to get into it later.
我之后会细说的。

196
00:10:58.900 --> 00:10:59.260
Okay.
好的。

197
00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:03.720
Well, you know, there are so many lists of the cringiest office episodes,
嗯，你知道，有很多关于《办公室》最尴尬剧集的榜单，

198
00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:06.320
and Pool Party never makes the liSt.
而《泳池派对》从来没上榜。

199
00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:11.260
However, I have to say after watching it, this one has moved to the top of the list for me.
不过，我不得不说，看完这一集后，它在我心目中已经跃居榜首了。

200
00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:14.180
I think before this, it was maybe Prince Family Paper.
我想在此之前，排第一的可能是《王子造纸公司》那一集。

201
00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:16.700
I found Garden Party quite cringey.
我觉得《花园派对》那一集挺尴尬的。

202
00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:20.180
I mean, Scott's Tots is moving down the list for me.
我的意思是，《斯科特的托特班》在我心里的尴尬排名正在下降。

203
00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:21.400
That's saying something.
那可是相当不容易了。

204
00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:21.940
I know.
我知道。

205
00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:25.140
I'm with you on the cringe factor on this one.
在尴尬程度上，我跟你感同身受。

206
00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:28.600
There's a few moments that I was like, wait, what?
有几个瞬间我当时就在想，等等，这是什么情况？

207
00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:30.080
Like I forgot happened.
就像我忘了发生过什么一样。

208
00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:33.940
I found an article on CheatSheet.com titled,
我在CheatSheet.com上看到一篇文章，标题是，

209
00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:36.540
How the Office Fans Feel About Pool Party.
《办公室》粉丝对《泳池派对》的看法。

210
00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:39.600
And it came out after this episode was released.
这篇文章是在这一集播出后发布的。

211
00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:43.940
I guess NBC's The Office Instagram had posted a clip from Pool Party,
我猜是NBC《办公室》的Instagram账号发了一段《泳池派对》的片段，

212
00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:47.500
and fans quickly took to the comments to name the episode
粉丝们很快就在评论区里把这一集称为

213
00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:50.180
the weirdest office episode in history.
《办公室》历史上最诡异的一集。

214
00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:52.640
One comment read,
其中一条评论写道，

215
00:11:52.980 --> 00:11:55.140
This episode was dot dot dot.
这一集真是……点点点。

216
00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:56.580
It was.
确实如此。

217
00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:58.760
Let's just leave it at that.
我们就说到这儿吧。

218
00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:02.460
I think that sums it up.
我觉得这总结得很到位。

219
00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:03.100
That's pretty good.
说得太好了。

220
00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:07.820
You know, I have a confession about this episode.
你知道吗，关于这一集我有个坦白。

221
00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:10.700
This episode, this was my first time watching it.
这一集，这是我第一次看。

222
00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:12.800
I did not watch it when it aired.
它播出的时候我没看。

223
00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:13.720
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

224
00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:17.980
Yeah, I experienced the dot dot dot for the very first time.
是的，我第一次体验到了那种“点点点”的感觉。

225
00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:20.000
It is truly cringey.
它确实非常尴尬。

226
00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:20.480
I know.
我知道。

227
00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:22.540
You know, I had read the table draft.
你知道，我读过剧本初稿。

228
00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:24.700
They still sent it to me on my maternity leave.
我休产假的时候他们还是把剧本发给我了。

229
00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:28.380
And, you know, I actually offered to call in for this episode.
而且，你知道，我其实主动提出过要为这一集打个电话客串。

230
00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:30.860
I thought Jim and Pam could have a phone call,
我想吉姆和帕姆可以通个电话，

231
00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.780
like maybe when Jim is trying to leave Robert's house.
比如吉姆正试图离开罗伯特家的时候。

232
00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:35.880
Yeah, like Pam's like, hey, where are you at?
对，就像帕姆问，嘿，你到哪儿了？

233
00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:37.560
Yes, when are you going to get home?
没错，你什么时候能到家？

234
00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:39.780
I thought that would put more pressure on him.
我觉得那样会给他施加更多压力。

235
00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:41.180
But the network said no.
但电视网拒绝了。

236
00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.060
They said you couldn't call in?
他们说你不能打电话客串？

237
00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:44.940
No, because then they'd have to pay me.
不，因为那样他们就得付我钱。

238
00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:45.460
Ew.
呃。

239
00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:46.320
Yeah.
是啊。

240
00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:48.420
But don't you think that would have been good?
但你不觉得那样会很好吗？

241
00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:49.040
I do.
我觉得会。

242
00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:52.020
If she's like, instead of just having no Pam in this episode?
如果她能出现，而不是这一集完全没有帕姆？

243
00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:52.780
I don't know.
我不知道。

244
00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:54.840
But no, they didn't go for it.
但不行，他们没采纳这个建议。

245
00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:57.640
I would have liked some Pam in this episode.
我本来希望这一集里能有帕姆的戏份。

246
00:12:57.860 --> 00:12:59.060
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

247
00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:00.440
I think so, too.
我也这么想。

248
00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.340
Well, maybe we should go to break.
好吧，也许我们该休息一下了。

249
00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:06.620
And then we'll come back and talk about this episode that I watched for the very first time.
回来之后我们再聊聊我第一次看的这一集。

250
00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:07.280
Okay.
好的。

251
00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:18.990
We are back.
我们回来了。

252
00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:23.030
This episode kicks off with a Jim prank.
这一集以吉姆的一个恶作剧开场。

253
00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:25.010
But who's really being pranked here?
但到底谁才是真正的受害者呢？

254
00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:26.070
Yes.
没错。

255
00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:31.650
Dwight returns to his desk, and he is disgusted when he realizes he sat on a meatball.
德怀特回到办公桌前，发现自己坐到了肉丸上，感到非常恶心。

256
00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:32.410
Yeah.
是啊。

257
00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:34.070
Stanley thinks that's hilarious.
斯坦利觉得这太搞笑了。

258
00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:36.830
And then Jim shares that without Pam,
然后吉姆说，如果没有帕姆在场，

259
00:13:37.090 --> 00:13:40.450
he doesn't really have an audience for his pranking of Dwight.
他捉弄德怀特时就没观众了。

260
00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:43.390
And that was half the fun until he found Stanley.
在发现斯坦利这个观众之前，那可是乐趣的一半来源。

261
00:13:43.890 --> 00:13:46.190
However, Stanley has very, very specific tastes.
然而，斯坦利的品味非常、非常独特。

262
00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:48.710
We see a little montage of a variety of pranks,
我们看到了一段各种恶作剧的剪辑，

263
00:13:48.850 --> 00:13:51.270
and there's only one thing that makes Stanley laugh,
只有一件事能让斯坦利发笑，

264
00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:53.650
and that is being meatballed.
那就是被肉丸砸中。

265
00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:57.810
Hashtag got meatballed.
标签：被肉丸砸了。

266
00:13:58.350 --> 00:14:03.090
Well, what we find out is basically Jim has been feeding Dwight and Stanley for weeks.
好吧，我们发现基本上吉姆已经喂了德怀特和斯坦利好几周了。

267
00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:06.350
This meatball prank, I mean, when does he have the time?
这个肉丸恶作剧，我是说，他哪来的时间？

268
00:14:06.350 --> 00:14:11.010
What is, by the way, Pam saying at home when Jim brings 36 meatballs to work
顺便问一下，当吉姆带了36个肉丸去上班，

269
00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:12.430
and puts them in Dwight's drawer?
并把它们放进德怀特的抽屉里时，帕姆在家会怎么说？

270
00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:15.690
We'll never know because I wasn't in the episode.
我们永远不会知道，因为我没参演这一集。

271
00:14:16.010 --> 00:14:17.810
Oh, it's going to keep coming back, guys.
噢，伙计们，这事儿还没完呢。

272
00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:23.290
I'll have you know one of the pranks we saw in that montage was a desk made out of Lego.
我得告诉你们，我们在剪辑里看到的其中一个恶作剧是乐高做的办公桌。

273
00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:25.650
Phil Shea had that desk made.
那是菲尔·谢伊做的。

274
00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:27.930
Steve Burgess said it was very delicate.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说那东西非常脆弱。

275
00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:29.230
It was.
确实如此。

276
00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:32.510
We could not get near it or touch it or it would fall apart immediately.
我们根本不能靠近或触碰它，否则它会立刻散架。

277
00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:34.790
Yeah, you couldn't really set anything on it.
没错，你根本没法在上面放任何东西。

278
00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:36.950
You can even see in the episode it dips down.
你甚至可以在剧里看到它往下塌陷。

279
00:14:37.150 --> 00:14:37.390
Yes.
是的。

280
00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:43.150
Phil was also in charge of all the meatballs and putting a stapler into a giant meatball.
菲尔还负责所有的肉丸，以及把订书机塞进一个巨大的肉丸里。

281
00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:48.450
I really want to see Phil Shea's to-do lists after he reads an episode.
我真想看看菲尔·谢伊读完剧本后的待办事项清单。

282
00:14:48.690 --> 00:14:50.770
Could you imagine finding one on the street?
你能想象在街上捡到一张吗？

283
00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:52.210
Have you seen those books?
你看过那些书吗？

284
00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:56.310
They're called, like, Found, and they're just, like, snippets of, like,
书名叫《发现》，里面全是些碎片，比如，

285
00:14:56.650 --> 00:15:00.870
