天哪，这场比赛太重要了。

1363
00:59:49.640 --> 00:59:54.640
This was the St. Louis Cardinals versus the Texas Rangers.
那是圣路易斯红雀队对阵德克萨斯游骑兵队。

1364
00:59:55.100 --> 00:59:56.820
And you know, Lee is from Texas.
你知道的，李是德克萨斯人。

1365
00:59:57.200 --> 00:59:57.480
Yes.
是的。

1366
00:59:57.760 --> 00:59:59.060
Well, my son was one month old.
当时我儿子才一个月大。

1367
00:59:59.060 --> 01:00:00.620
My sister came out to visit.
我姐姐来看望我们。

1368
01:00:00.840 --> 01:00:03.720
She brought all kinds of Cardinals gear for my son to wear.
她带了各种红雀队的装备给我儿子穿。

1369
01:00:03.960 --> 01:00:09.560
And Lee and I had an agreement where we either had to alternate the St. Louis Cardinals onesie
李和我达成了一个协议，我们要么轮流给他穿圣路易斯红雀队的连体衣

1370
01:00:09.560 --> 01:00:13.640
and the Texas Rangers onesie, or he had to wear a little bit of each team.
和德克萨斯游骑兵队的连体衣，要么就让他两队的衣服都穿一点。

1371
01:00:14.600 --> 01:00:15.080
Aw.
噢。

1372
01:00:15.080 --> 01:00:15.200
Aw.
噢。

1373
01:00:15.480 --> 01:00:20.300
So listen, game six of that World Series is epic because of David Freese.
听着，那届世界大赛的第六场比赛因为大卫·弗里斯而变得史诗级。

1374
01:00:20.480 --> 01:00:22.740
I won't go on and on, but oh my gosh.
我不会没完没了地说下去，但天哪。

1375
01:00:22.860 --> 01:00:28.540
First of all, he ties it up, and then he has a walk-off homer in the 11th inning for them
首先，他追平了比分，然后在第11局打出了再见全垒打，帮助他们

1376
01:00:28.540 --> 01:00:31.920
to win that game, which they needed to win in order to get to the seventh game.
赢得了那场比赛，而他们必须赢下那场才能进入第七场决胜局。

1377
01:00:32.560 --> 01:00:39.100
For the seventh game of the World Series, I sneaked two Cardinals socks on my son's feet.
在世界大赛的第七场，我偷偷给我儿子的脚上穿了两只红雀队的袜子。

1378
01:00:39.220 --> 01:00:40.300
And the Cardinals won!
结果红雀队赢了！

1379
01:00:40.300 --> 01:00:41.640
And I think that's why.
我觉得就是因为这个。

1380
01:00:43.680 --> 01:00:45.280
I love Arlington Stadium.
我喜欢阿灵顿体育场。

1381
01:00:45.300 --> 01:00:46.880
We would go there and watch ballgames.
我们以前常去那里看球赛。

1382
01:00:47.000 --> 01:00:47.500
It's beautiful.
那里很美。

1383
01:00:47.700 --> 01:00:49.400
You're making me want to go to a baseball game.
你让我都想去看棒球比赛了。

1384
01:00:49.540 --> 01:00:50.000
I know.
我也是。

1385
01:00:50.500 --> 01:00:51.780
Well, listen, everybody.
好了，听着，各位。

1386
01:00:52.040 --> 01:00:53.340
That was pool party.
刚才那是泳池派对。

1387
01:00:53.520 --> 01:00:59.940
But before we leave, I think we need to have a birthday party.
但在我们离开之前，我觉得我们需要办个生日派对。

1388
01:01:00.360 --> 01:01:00.840
What?
什么？

1389
01:01:01.280 --> 01:01:07.120
Because, Angela Kinsey, we are recording this episode right before we go on our summer break.
因为安吉拉·金赛，我们在暑假前夕录制这一集。

1390
01:01:07.220 --> 01:01:09.300
Your birthday is June 25th.
你的生日是6月25日。

1391
01:01:09.300 --> 01:01:11.980
And we're going to be on vacation for your birthday.
而你过生日的时候我们正好在度假。

1392
01:01:12.800 --> 01:01:16.320
I hope I did a good job as party coordinator this time.
希望这次我作为派对协调员表现得不错。

1393
01:01:16.480 --> 01:01:18.220
I can't believe you remembered this.
真不敢相信你还记得这个。

1394
01:01:18.300 --> 01:01:21.640
I also can't believe I almost forgot to pick you up this morning.
我也真不敢相信我今天早上差点忘了去接你。

1395
01:01:21.840 --> 01:01:22.380
I know.
我知道。

1396
01:01:22.840 --> 01:01:24.460
I've been driving Jenna to work.
我一直在开车送珍娜上班。

1397
01:01:24.560 --> 01:01:25.300
We've been carpooling.
我们一直在拼车。

1398
01:01:25.380 --> 01:01:26.300
It's been so fun.
这太有趣了。

1399
01:01:26.320 --> 01:01:28.540
I've really enjoyed it because of my broken shoulder.
因为我的肩膀骨折了，我真的很享受这个过程。

1400
01:01:28.760 --> 01:01:33.020
And this morning I was on autopilot, and I just got on the freeway and went the wrong way.
今天早上我处于自动驾驶模式，直接上了高速公路，结果走错了方向。

1401
01:01:33.660 --> 01:01:35.300
I was so worried.
我刚才担心死了。

1402
01:01:35.300 --> 01:01:37.160
How am I going to hide the birthday stuff?
我该怎么把生日的东西藏起来呢？

1403
01:01:37.400 --> 01:01:39.040
Because you're driving me to work.
因为你要开车送我去上班。

1404
01:01:39.040 --> 01:01:40.880
So that's why I had a giant bag with me today.
所以这就是我今天带了个大包的原因。

1405
01:01:41.020 --> 01:01:41.700
You didn't ask.
你当时没问。

1406
01:01:41.880 --> 01:01:42.340
Thank goodness.
谢天谢地。

1407
01:01:42.780 --> 01:01:44.280
Here's your present, Ange.
这是你的礼物，安吉。

1408
01:01:44.380 --> 01:01:45.420
You're so sweet.
你真贴心。

1409
01:01:45.420 --> 01:01:46.540
I can't believe this.
我简直不敢相信。

1410
01:01:46.640 --> 01:01:47.600
This is so cute.
这太可爱了。

1411
01:01:48.480 --> 01:01:49.300
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1412
01:01:49.400 --> 01:01:51.480
I didn't do my hair or anything today.
我今天头发都没弄，什么都没做。

1413
01:01:51.480 --> 01:01:51.540
I know.
我知道。

1414
01:01:51.620 --> 01:01:52.260
I thought of that.
我考虑到了。

1415
01:01:52.340 --> 01:01:53.940
You said I didn't have time to get ready.
你说我没时间打扮。

1416
01:01:54.100 --> 01:01:55.580
I'm going to show up in my pajamas.
我打算穿着睡衣就去了。

1417
01:01:55.580 --> 01:01:58.380
And I was like, well, we might be taking some pictures.
当时我就想，好吧，我们可能会拍些照片。

1418
01:01:58.520 --> 01:01:59.680
You got me a succulent?
你给我买了盆多肉植物？

1419
01:02:00.020 --> 01:02:00.460
Of course.
当然。

1420
01:02:00.620 --> 01:02:01.060
Aw.
噢。

1421
01:02:01.380 --> 01:02:01.720
Wait.
等等。

1422
01:02:01.880 --> 01:02:03.020
I got to fish it out.
我得把它掏出来。

1423
01:02:03.320 --> 01:02:07.860
I didn't get you any, like, birthday sweet treat because I know Josh does that.
我没给你买什么生日甜点，因为我知道乔什会准备。

1424
01:02:07.940 --> 01:02:09.320
You have plenty of sweet treats.
你已经有很多甜点了。

1425
01:02:09.500 --> 01:02:10.460
Oh, the pen is mine.
噢，这支笔是我的。

1426
01:02:10.760 --> 01:02:11.240
Sorry.
抱歉。

1427
01:02:14.100 --> 01:02:16.180
Oh, this is so cute.
噢，这太可爱了。

1428
01:02:16.220 --> 01:02:17.880
I love a succulent.
我超爱多肉植物。

1429
01:02:18.460 --> 01:02:19.720
And you got me something.
而且你还给我买了别的东西。

1430
01:02:19.980 --> 01:02:21.720
You got me a little piece of...
你给我买了一小件……

1431
01:02:21.720 --> 01:02:22.980
What is it?
是什么？

1432
01:02:23.880 --> 01:02:24.840
You guys.
你们这些人啊。

1433
01:02:25.580 --> 01:02:27.340
It's a hummingbird necklace.
是一条蜂鸟项链。

1434
01:02:27.760 --> 01:02:29.860
It's a little gold hummingbird.
是一只小金蜂鸟。

1435
01:02:30.100 --> 01:02:32.680
It is so freaking cute.
这简直太可爱了。

1436
01:02:32.680 --> 01:02:34.520
I love it so much.
我太喜欢了。

1437
01:02:34.520 --> 01:02:35.960
I'm putting it on right now.
我现在就戴上。

1438
01:02:36.300 --> 01:02:37.720
Hummingbirds and succulents.
蜂鸟和多肉植物。

1439
01:02:37.960 --> 01:02:38.920
Equal Angela.
这就是安吉拉。

1440
01:02:39.180 --> 01:02:40.960
And we've got a card out there for you, too.
我们在外面还给你准备了一张卡片。

1441
01:02:41.140 --> 01:02:42.100
Everyone signed it.
大家都签名了。

1442
01:02:42.400 --> 01:02:42.620
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1443
01:02:42.620 --> 01:02:43.640
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1444
01:02:43.800 --> 01:02:44.760
Thank you, guys.
谢谢你们。

1445
01:02:45.260 --> 01:02:45.560
Aw.
噢。

1446
01:02:45.760 --> 01:02:46.940
Happy birthday, Angela.
生日快乐，安吉拉。

1447
01:02:47.220 --> 01:02:48.340
Happy pool party.
泳池派对快乐。

1448
01:02:48.700 --> 01:02:51.700
Thank you, Steve Burgess and Ellie Kemper and Amina.
谢谢史蒂夫·伯吉斯、艾丽·坎伯和阿米娜。

1449
01:02:52.140 --> 01:02:55.560
And Matt Flynn and all of you guys for writing in with your questions.
还有马特·弗林以及所有写信提问的你们。

1450
01:02:56.240 --> 01:02:57.520
We love you guys.
我们爱你们。

1451
01:02:57.740 --> 01:02:59.120
Oh, oh, lady, wait.
噢，噢，女士，等等。

1452
01:02:59.220 --> 01:02:59.400
What?
什么？

1453
01:02:59.540 --> 01:03:01.160
One more thing before we go.
我们走之前还有件事。

1454
01:03:01.700 --> 01:03:04.900
This episode is going to be airing in AuguSt.
这一集将在八月播出。

1455
01:03:05.420 --> 01:03:05.820
August?
八月？

1456
01:03:06.360 --> 01:03:06.820
Yes.
是的。

1457
01:03:06.980 --> 01:03:12.900
So we should remind everyone about our live show that's going to be in Toronto on September
所以我们应该提醒大家，我们九月份在多伦多有一场现场演出，

1458
01:03:12.900 --> 01:03:15.660
21st as part of the Just for Laughs Festival.
时间是21号，作为“欢笑节”的一部分。

1459
01:03:15.900 --> 01:03:16.460
Oh, yes.
噢，对。

1460
01:03:16.460 --> 01:03:17.680
We are so excited.
我们太兴奋了。

1461
01:03:17.860 --> 01:03:18.640
So excited.
超级兴奋。

1462
01:03:18.640 --> 01:03:22.880
We had such a blast at Just for Laughs in Vancouver, and we can't wait to do it again.
我们在温哥华的“欢笑节”玩得太开心了，迫不及待想再来一次。

1463
01:03:23.160 --> 01:03:23.500
Yes.
没错。

1464
01:03:23.600 --> 01:03:24.760
And tickets are still available.
而且票还有剩。

1465
01:03:25.060 --> 01:03:27.220
I'll put a link in Office Ladies Pod Stories.
我会把链接放在《办公室女士》的播客故事里。

1466
01:03:27.600 --> 01:03:27.980
Great.
太棒了。

1467
01:03:28.260 --> 01:03:28.480
Okay.
好的。

1468
01:03:28.820 --> 01:03:30.100
Now we can go.
现在我们可以走了。

1469
01:03:30.360 --> 01:03:30.800
Bye.
再见。

1470
01:03:31.340 --> 01:03:31.720
Bye.
再见。

1471
01:03:39.190 --> 01:03:41.290
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1472
01:03:41.550 --> 01:03:45.690
Office Ladies is produced by Earwolf, Jenna Fisher, and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》由Earwolf、珍娜·费舍和安吉拉·金赛制作。

1473
01:03:45.890 --> 01:03:48.070
Our senior producer is Cassie Jerkins.
我们的高级制作人是卡西·杰金斯。

1474
01:03:48.250 --> 01:03:50.350
Our in-studio engineer is Sam Kiefer.
我们的演播室工程师是萨姆·基弗。

1475
01:03:50.490 --> 01:03:52.730
Our editing and mixing engineer is Jordan Duffy.
我们的剪辑和混音工程师是乔丹·达菲。

1476
01:03:52.970 --> 01:03:55.070
And our associate producer is Ainsley Bubico.
我们的助理制作人是安斯利·布比科。

1477
01:03:55.390 --> 01:03:58.210
Our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
我们的主题曲是克里德·布拉顿演唱的《橡胶树》。

1478
01:03:58.210 --> 01:03:59.150
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。
